From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Subject: [PATCH] kk: retain the real slice for overflowing non-array 2D views

STEAMAC-G sub-pattern A includes three requests for a single-layer 2D
RGBA8 image, extent 1920x288 or 1952x288, flags 0x8, usage 0x480097,
with a 2D view of mips 0+1 and layers 0+65536. Patch 0065 rejects these;
Venus creates views asynchronously so the next vkCmdBeginRendering fails
an object-type-14 lookup and kills the guest context.

A non-array 2D view of a single-layer 2D image can only address its one
real slice. Normalize an explicit count greater than one to that slice
before common Vulkan initialization and Metal's uint16 narrowing. Do not
change empty ranges, non-zero base layers, arrays, 3D views or REMAINING.
No format or backing allocation is substituted.

Zink's create_ivci forms layerCount as 1 + last_layer - first_layer,
where pipe_surface's layers are 16-bit; last_layer == 65535 produces the
captured 65536 without a protocol width conversion. Its resource usage
construction also produces the captured HOST_TRANSFER/FEEDBACK_LOOP mask.
The guest process and the cause of the bad pipe_surface remain unproven;
this is a safe host recovery, not a claim to fix that guest producer.

Repro: image_views.c, sentry-wide-1920 / sentry-wide-1952 and a usage-pNext
control. The baseline returns VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED. With this
patch each creates, clears via dynamic rendering and reads back every
RGBA8 byte under Metal API validation. All thirteen original cases pass.

Generated-by: LLM
---
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_view.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_view.c
@@ -55,6 +55,29 @@
 {
    VK_FROM_HANDLE(kk_image, image, pCreateInfo->image);
    const VkImageSubresourceRange *range = &pCreateInfo->subresourceRange;
+
+   /* A non-array 2D view of a single-layer 2D image can only name that one
+    * slice. Zink can send 65536 when a uint16_t last_layer underflows. Keep
+    * the real slice rather than narrowing the count to zero in Metal or
+    * failing an asynchronous Venus object creation. Do not manufacture a
+    * slice for empty ranges, or change array and 3D view semantics. */
+   VkImageViewCreateInfo normalized_info;
+   if (image->vk.image_type == VK_IMAGE_TYPE_2D &&
+       image->vk.array_layers == 1 &&
+       pCreateInfo->viewType == VK_IMAGE_VIEW_TYPE_2D &&
+       range->baseArrayLayer == 0 && range->layerCount > 1 &&
+       range->layerCount != VK_REMAINING_ARRAY_LAYERS) {
+      char app[256];
+      kk_device_app_name(dev, app, sizeof(app));
+      mesa_loge("kk: %s: clamping non-array image view layers %u to 1 "
+                "(image %ux%u, format %u, view format %u)",
+                app, range->layerCount, image->vk.extent.width,
+                image->vk.extent.height, image->vk.format, pCreateInfo->format);
+      normalized_info = *pCreateInfo;
+      normalized_info.subresourceRange.layerCount = 1;
+      pCreateInfo = &normalized_info;
+      range = &pCreateInfo->subresourceRange;
+   }
 
    /* Mesa's common initializer resolves REMAINING_* but only asserts validity.
     * In release builds an empty range (including base == size with REMAINING)
